# Intent: The Brain route and a clean way out of the hosted brain (owner question 2026-11-18). self.brain.set_route custom does, in order: stop the vendor check, activation and connect at once (a flag every loop looks at); erase every NVS namespace that starts with cl_ (the vendor link's address, token, activation state, MQTT settings), and nothing else: the host pairing, the privacy bits and the chip's key blocks are never touched or read out; save route custom; show one plain line on the screen, silently (Hosted link removed. To stop your account keeping this robot, remove it in the vendor's console); push the event brain_route {route custom, hosted_removed true} for the dashboard; and restart the unit four seconds later so no vendor timer, task or RAM copy survives. The saved route also keeps a cloudtest image from activating again at the next start. self.brain.status answers the route, the number of cl_ keys and the number of attempts to reach the vendor service since the start (so a bench check can show there were none). The factory reset already erases cl_ (it is not on the keep list); a test pins that. What the unit cannot remove: the device's binding in the vendor's account and any voice history the vendor holds (the doc says so).
# Placement: unit
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal/maipai_hosted.cc, maipai_hosted.h and maipai_hosted_core.h (ours); hooks in ota.cc, application.cc and websocket_protocol.cc of the xiaozhi-esp32 tree (MIT)
# Check after a flash: on the cloudtest image after a hosted session, self.brain.status shows cl_keys above 0; self.brain.set_route custom shows the line, sends brain_route, restarts; after the restart self.brain.status answers route custom, cl_keys 0, vendor_attempts 0, and ten minutes later vendor_attempts is still 0; flashing plain then brings the host link back with the old pairing; a factory reset leaves no cl_ keys.
# Kconfig: none
# Memory cost: none while idle in any image beyond about 600 bytes of flash and a few bytes of flags; the leave path uses a short-lived vector of namespace names (under 200 bytes) and one esp_timer for the restart.

